l</surname><given-names>RT</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>The number of partners.</article-title>  <person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Lauman</surname><given-names>EO</given-names></name><name><surname>Gagnon</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Michael</surname><given-names>RT</given-names></name><name><surname>Michaels</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group>, eds. <source>The social organization of sexuality: sexual practices in the United States</source>. <publisher-loc>Chicago and London</publisher-loc>: <publisher-name>The University of Chicago Press</publisher-name>, <year>1994</year>:<fpage>172</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>224</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b20"><label>20</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Carael</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>Sexual behaviour.</article-title>  <person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Cleland</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Ferry</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group>, eds. <source>Sexual behaviour and AIDS in the developing world</source>. <publisher-loc>London</publisher-loc>: <publisher-name>Taylor &#x00026; Francis</publisher-name>, <year>1995</year>:<fpage>75</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>123</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b21"><label>21</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wellings</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Collumbien</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Slaymaker</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Sexual behaviour in context: global perspective.</article-title> <source>Lancet</source> <year>2006</year>;<volume>368</volume>:<fpage>1706</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>28</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1