-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Rodrigues</surname><given-names>LC</given-names></name><name><surname>Wellings</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Increased condom use at sexual debout in the general population of Slovenia and association with subsequent condom use.</article-title> <source>AIDS</source> <year>2005</year>;<volume>19</volume>:<fpage>1215</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>23</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15990576</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b26"><label>26</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gremy</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Beltzer</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>HIV risk and condom use in the adult heterosexual population in France between 1992 and 2001: return to the starting point?</article-title> <source>AIDS</source> <year>2004</year>;<volume>26</volume>:<fpage>805</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15075517</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b27"><label>27</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Magnus</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>Risk behaviours and risk context.</article-title>  <person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Hubert</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Bajos</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Sandfort</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group>, eds. <source>Sexual behaviour and HIV/AIDS in Europe</source>. <publisher-loc>London</publisher-loc>: <publisher-name>UCL Press</publisher-name>, <year>1998</year>:<fpage>199</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>218</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b28"><label>28</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Olson</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Browning</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Sampling procedures and data quality.</article-title>  <person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Laumann</surname><given-names>EO</given-names></name><name><surname>Gagnon</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Michael</surname><given-names>RT</given-names></name><name><surname>Michaels</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group>, eds. <source>The social organization of sexuality: sexual practices in the United States</source>. <publisher-loc>Chicago</publisher-loc>: <publisher-name>University of Chicago Press</publisher-name>, <year>1994</year>:<fpage>549</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>70</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b29"><label>29</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Biggar</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Melbye</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>Responses to anonymous questionnaires concerning sexual behavior: a method to examine potential biases.</article-title> <source>Am J Public Health</source> <year>1992</year>;<volume>82</volume>:<fpage>1506</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>12</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1443301</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>